{"shortname": "maxima", "name": "Maxima -- GPL CAS based on DOE-MACSYMA", "_id": "50a93871271846176dfc866f", "url": "https://sourceforge.net/p/maxima/", "private": false, "short_description": "Maxima is a computer algebra system comparable to commercial systems like Mathematica and Maple. It emphasizes symbolic mathematical computation: algebra, trigonometry, calculus, and much more.\r\n\r\nFor example, Maxima solves x^2-r*x-s^2-r*s=0, giving the symbolic results [x=r+s, x=-s]. It can also calculate with exact integers and fractions, native floating-point, and high-precision big floats.\r\n\r\nMaxima has user-friendly front-ends, an online manual, plotting commands, and numerical libraries. It features its own programming language, and many users have contributed useful packages in various areas over the decades. It is GPL-licensed and largely written in Common Lisp. Executables can be downloaded for Windows, Mac, Linux, and Android; source code is also available. An active community maintains and extends the system. \r\n\r\nWebsite: https://maxima.sourceforge.io\r\n\r\nAdditional add-on packages for Maxima can be found at: https://github.com/maxima-project-on-github/maxima-packages", "creation_date": "2000-04-23", "summary": "Computer Algebra System written in Common Lisp", "external_homepage": "https://maxima.sourceforge.io", "video_url": null, "socialnetworks": [{"accounturl": null, "socialnetwork": "Twitter"}, {"accounturl": null, "socialnetwork": "Facebook"}, {"accounturl": null, "socialnetwork": "Fediverse"}, {"accounturl": null, "socialnetwork": "Instagram"}], "status": "active", "moved_to_url": "", "preferred_support_tool": "_url", "preferred_support_url": "http://maxima.sourceforge.net/maximalist.html", "developers": [{"username": "macrakis", "name": "Stavros Macrakis", "url": "https://sourceforge.net/u/macrakis/"}, {"username": "tomasriker", "name": "David Scherfgen", "url": "https://sourceforge.net/u/tomasriker/"}, {"username": "van_nek", "name": "Volker 